  "id": "DrugBank_DB09074 - MONDO_3795",
  "verbalization": "Olaparib, a poly (ADP-ribose) polymerase (PARP) inhibitor, is associated with multiple indications that ultimately lead to Ovarian Small Cell Carcinoma (OSCPC). The evidence suggests that Olaparib may exert its therapeutic effect through a mechanism that involves the targeting of tumor cells with a shared pathway or molecular signature. The indirect pathways connect Olaparib to Tretamine, which in turn is linked to OSCPC, indicating a potential role in the treatment of ovarian tumors through a shared biological process. The presence of multiple indirect pathways, each involving different indications and mechanisms, suggests that the relationship between Olaparib and OSCPC may be mediated through a common downstream effect, such as the inhibition of tumor cell proliferation or survival. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship, emphasizing the importance of understanding the underlying molecular mechanisms that connect these entities.",
